.TH G3PROBE 1
.SH NAME
g3probe \- compare the 3-D providers on one face at a time
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B g3probe
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I G3probe
draws the same small scenes through
.B /dis/math/draw3d.dis
and
.B /dis/math/draw3ddev.dis
and counts what lands, so that a difference between the two is a number
rather than an impression.
It exists because
.IR draw3dbench (1)
checks the GPU's flat
.B fillpoly3
for placement, scale, rotation, occlusion and equal depth, and checks
.B fillpoly3g
\- the per-vertex entry point that
.IR gorge (1)
and
.IR strider (1)
are built almost entirely on \- for nothing but whether it shades.
.PP
Four measurements, each for both providers:
.TP
depth
one quad at six depths, through
.B fillpoly3
and
.BR fillpoly3g ,
lit pixels each.
The two entry points must agree.
.TP
occlusion
a near green quad and a far red one, drawn in both orders, through
.B frustum
and through
.BR frustumoffset .
With a working depth buffer the order cannot matter.
.TP
scale
a corridor of 1 to 256 faces, the shape
.I gorge
draws.
.TP
frames
the same corridor drawn over one frame and over eight, with a present
between each.
.TP
model
the corridor again with a non-identity model matrix, since everything
else leaves it at identity and the games do not.
.TP
eye plane
a wall running from behind the eye to well in front, as
.IR gorge (1)'s
canyon does every frame, with
.B fillpoly3g
and with
.BR line3 .
.PP
It also writes the first device frame to
.B g3probe.raw
as raw pixels in the display's format, for looking at.
.SH RESULTS
Placement, the depth test,
.BR frustumoffset ,
a model transform and two hundred and fifty-six faces all agree between
providers to within about 1%, which is rasterisation.
.PP
The two that did not are why this exists.
A wall crossing the eye plane lit 40596 pixels through software and
.B 185898
through Metal until
.I devdraw
was made to clip Gouraud polygons the way it always clipped flat ones;
it is 40290 now.
And
.B line3
still does not clip in either provider, where they fail in opposite
directions \- software draws nothing, the device draws something.
.PP
The fourth does not:
.IP
.EX
provider       frames        lit
software            1      23376
device              1          0
device              1          0
device              1      23154
device              1      23154
device              1      23154
device              1          0
device              1      23154
device              1          0
software            8      23376
device              8      23154      (4 runs, all)
.EE
.PP
**One frame drawn and read gives nothing at all about half the time.**
Eight frames is right every time, and the software provider is right
every time.
.PP
The cause is in
.B /doc/draw3d-adoption-plan.md:
presentation consumes the geometry queue without writing the softscreen
back, so whether a frame's 3-D ever reaches the image everything else
reads is a race between the present and the next readback.
Over several frames a readback eventually wins; over one it may not.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/g3probe.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR draw3dbench (1),
.IR framegrab (1),
.IR gorge (1)
.PP
.B /doc/draw3d-adoption-plan.md
.SH BUGS
It needs a window and no window manager: with no
.I wm
the display is what the program drew into, which is what makes reading
it back mean anything.
.PP
It flushes before every read.
Without that it measures the screen as it stood before the drawing, and
an early version of this reported a first-call fault that was entirely
its own missing flush.
.PP
Nothing here asserts.
It prints numbers for a person to compare, because two of the four
measurements have no single right answer to check against \- only the
other provider.
